## Claim
Text: "Daughters of President Muhammadu Buhari and Vice President Yemi Osinbajo brought about the dissolution of Special Anti-Robbery Squad (SARS)."
Claim date: October 12, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20201101095614/https://authorityngr.com/2020/10/12/how-buhari-osinbajos-daughters-brought-sars-down/

## Initial Q&A
### What specific, public actions did the daughters of President Muhammadu Buhari and Vice President Yemi Osinbajo take that are cited as contributing to the dissolution of SARS?
Answer: The specific public actions cited were that both Zahra Buhari and Kiki Osinbajo posted a viral image showing three fists with the hashtag "#EndPoliceBrutality" on their Instagram stories to join and amplify the End SARS protests.

Source URL: https://dailypost.ng/2020/10/10/end-sars-zahra-buhari-kiki-osinbajo-join-protest/

### What was the official announcement made by the Nigerian government on October 11, 2020, regarding SARS, and what reasons were provided for that decision?
Answer: On October 11, 2020, the Nigerian government officially announced the dissolution of the Special Anti-Robbery Squad (SARS). The Inspector General of Police issued a tweet stating, “The Inspector General of Police has dissolved the Special Anti-Robbery Squad (SARS) across the Thirty-Six (36) State Commands and the Federal Capital Territory (FCT) with immediate effects.” This decision was made in response to massive nationwide protests by citizens, particularly young people, who were demonstrating against the unit’s notorious use of "brute force," including "consistent harassment, killing, torture, unfair criminal profiling and unlawful arrests."

Source URL: https://citinewsroom.com/2020/10/endsars-nigerias-notorious-police-unit-dissolved-after-citizens-protests/

